description:
**What:** Create crate-jmap-mail-client/tests/helpers.rs with shared test infrastructure used by all three EmailSubmission wiremock test files.

**Algorithm:**
1. Create crate-jmap-mail-client/tests/helpers.rs.
2. Add the following (non-test, pub) helper:

```rust
use wiremock::MockServer;

/// Build a jmap_base_client::Session whose apiUrl points at the mock server.
/// One account: A13824 / john@example.com, primary for urn:ietf:params:jmap:mail.
/// Oracle: RFC 8620 §2.1 example session JSON shape.
pub fn make_session(server: &MockServer) -> jmap_base_client::Session {
    let json = serde_json::json!({
        "capabilities": {
            "urn:ietf:params:jmap:core": {},
            "urn:ietf:params:jmap:mail": {}
        },
        "accounts": {
            "A13824": {
                "name": "john@example.com",
                "isPersonal": true,
                "isReadOnly": false,
                "accountCapabilities": { "urn:ietf:params:jmap:mail": {} }
            }
        },
        "primaryAccounts": { "urn:ietf:params:jmap:mail": "A13824" },
        "username": "john@example.com",
        "apiUrl": format!("{}/api/", server.uri()),
        "downloadUrl": format!("{}/dl/{{accountId}}/{{blobId}}/{{name}}?accept={{type}}", server.uri()),
        "uploadUrl": format!("{}/ul/{{accountId}}/", server.uri()),
        "eventSourceUrl": format!("{}/sse/?types={{types}}&closeafter={{closeafter}}&ping={{ping}}", server.uri()),
        "state": "s1"
    });
    serde_json::from_value(json).expect("make_session: session must deserialize")
}

/// Build a SessionClient pointed at the mock server.
pub async fn make_client(server: &MockServer) -> jmap_mail_client::SessionClient {
    let client = jmap_base_client::JmapClient::new(
        jmap_base_client::auth::DefaultTransport,
        jmap_base_client::auth::NoneAuth,
        &server.uri(),
        jmap_base_client::client::ClientConfig::default(),
    ).expect("make_client: JmapClient construction must succeed");
    use jmap_mail_client::JmapMailExt;
    client.with_mail_session(make_session(server))
}
```

3. Add a compile-check test to confirm the helper builds:
```rust
#[tokio::test]
async fn helpers_compile() {
    let server = wiremock::MockServer::start().await;
    let _sc = make_client(&server).await;
}
```

4. Run: cargo test -p jmap-mail-client 2>&1 | grep -E '(ok|FAILED|error)'

**Defensive programming rules:**
- No unwrap() without explanatory comment; use .expect("reason") in test helpers
- No network calls to real servers — all URLs point to MockServer
- make_session must take &MockServer (not a URI string) so the server lifetime is enforced by the borrow checker

**Tests:**
- helpers_compile: confirms make_session and make_client build and the session deserializes; oracle is the RFC 8620 §2.1 session shape

**Acceptance criteria:**
- tests/helpers.rs exists and is accessible via #[path] or mod declaration from test files
- cargo test -p jmap-mail-client exits 0
- cargo clippy -p jmap-mail-client -- -D warnings exits 0
